Kompakt: ordered (Bayer) dithering as an option, kompakt_wf_dither

meink has one dither algorithm, Floyd-Steinberg, run on every frame; its
dither_type node is on or off and dither_param changes nothing visible.
Error diffusion re-decides every pixel from its neighbours, so a moving
picture boils and scrolling text crawls. An ordered matrix decides each
pixel from its position alone: the pattern stands still between frames
and a changed region changes only where the picture did.

The loader already wraps meink's frame entry (eink_update_screen) for the
sleep image, and meink copies the frame it is handed (renderWriteImage
memcpy), so the loader dithers into its own 32-bit copy and passes that.
meink greys a pixel as the sum of its three low bytes; the copy holds
pure 0 or 255 in all three, which every gamma and contrast maps to black
and white. Every dither request (the app's dither_type write, Auto's
moving and settled phases) goes through kompakt_set_dither: with
kompakt_wf_dither set, meink's dithering stays off and the loader's
Bayer pass is on for exactly the frames that would have been FS dithered.
0 is stock (meink FS), 1 Bayer 8x8 (64 levels), 2 Bayer 4x4 (coarser),
3 the hybrid below.
A write re-routes the current state and repaints. Off by default.

kompakt_wf_dither_cut takes "lo hi" on a 0..255 grey (default 48 208):
at or below lo is black, at or above hi is white, and only the greys in
between are patterned, so near-white backgrounds and the light edge
pixels of text stay clean. The matrix is spread over that range.

3 is ordered error diffusion (J. van der Zwan): Atkinson's diffusion,
which passes on 6/8 of each pixel's error and so keeps highlights and
shadows clean, rounding against a Bayer 8x8 threshold held near the
middle. kompakt_wf_dither_step sets that spread (0 plain Atkinson, 32
full Bayer, default 8). Greys outside the cut range are pure and pass no
error on, so text and white backgrounds stay clean here too.

